@bank all
// FX28 (2026-10-26, the user's playtest notes: the Tier 2 test and the promotion "very very hard to miss"; lead 38's
// plan A-G), for 24p's worksText with PROMO_BEATS_ON. Drafted by FX28 in the house voice, for SW2 to polish. Calder
// speaks unless noted: exact, numbers not adjectives, never "well done" (her arc's payoff), no "!". Mails are
// "Subject | body", unsigned (the game adds the sender). {day}: "tomorrow" or a weekday; {time}: a time like 08:15.

// the board's gold ring on the test's Take it (forced, whatever Teaching arrows says)
== pb.ptr.test
- Your Tier 2 test: take it

// the Schedule's and Tracked's rows, said by nobody
== pb.row.test
- Your Tier 2 test
== pb.row.result
- Your result with the Chief
== pb.row.pip
- Your pip, from the Captain
== pb.row.cabin
- Your new cabin, after dinner

// A: the evening before, from up to two friends (Mail, 20:00; one each)
== mail.pb.luck
- Good luck | Big day tomorrow. You'll be fine. You've done harder jobs than this one with half the bay watching.
- Tomorrow | Heard about your test. Get some sleep and eat a proper breakfast. That's an order, from a friend.
// A: the test morning, once you're up (a device notice, said by nobody)
== pb.morning.notice
- Today: your Tier 2 test, 09:00. It goes up on the job board in the Works bay.
// A: Calder, as you come into the bay that morning (her own lines under flag pb.promo.morning come first)
== pb.morning.say
- Morning. Your test's on the board at nine. Take it when you're ready.

// B: holding another job while the test waits on the board (a notice, once an hour; {time}: when the test comes off)
== pb.busy.notice
- Your Tier 2 test waits on the job board till {time}. Turn in or drop this job first.

// C: passed. Her word at the turn-in, the Mail, the notice
== pb.passed.say
- That's the test done. Your result {day}, first thing. My office, {time}.
== mail.pb.passed
- Your test | Done. Your result {day}, {time}, my office. Not before.
== pb.passed.notice
- Your Tier 2 test is done. Your result: {day}, {time}, the Chief's office.

// D: the result day. The Mail at 06:00, the notice once you're up, and her toast at 08:00 (pb.promo.summons)
== mail.pb.result
- Your result | My office, {time}. Before your shift. Clock in on the way if you like.
== pb.result.notice
- Your Tier 2 result: {time}, the Chief's office, Works bay. Before your shift.
== pb.promo.summons
- Chief Calder: My office, 08:15. Your result. — C.
// her words by Mail if you never came to her office (promo.mail's switch-on twin)
== mail.pb.promo
- Your result | You weren't about, so you'll read it instead. You passed. As of today you're an Officer: Technician, Tier 2. Your badge is on my desk. The Captain pins your pip this afternoon, observation room. Clean uniform. Ten minutes early.

// E: the pip, the same day (the Captain's Mail after the result; the invite; the notice 30 minutes before)
== mail.pb.captain
- Congratulations | Chief Calder tells me you've passed. I'd like to pin your pip myself: this afternoon, in the observation room on Deck 1. Bring one honest answer: what should an officer never forget? I'll ask.
== mail.pb.invite
- Your pip, {time} | Today at {time}, the observation room, Deck 1. The Captain pins your pip. Clean uniform. It takes ten minutes. There will be tea.
== pb.pip.notice
- The Captain pins your pip at {time}: the observation room, Deck 1. Go now.
== pb.pip.say
- It's nearly time. Up to Deck 1. Don't keep the Captain waiting.

// F: your cabin after dinner. The notice as she sets off to find you ({name}: Calder, or Vance), and her word when she reaches you
== pb.move.notice
- Your cabin, 4-23: {name} is coming to find you and take you there.
== pb.walk.met
- There you are. Your cabin, then. With me.
// Calder's Mail at 17:00
== mail.pb.cabin
- Your cabin | After dinner I'll walk you to 4-23. Eat first. Your things are on their way.
